\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 923 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA EMPLOYMENT SOARS, PUSHES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO 2-YEAR HIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's jobs market continued to surge in September, when it added 49,500 new jobs, a figure that sent the Australian dollar to fresh two-year highs and puts pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to resume its tightening policy. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN: CAN'T TOLERATE EXCESSIVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan said Thursday that the government won't tolerate excessive moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, adding that decisive steps to deal with the strong yen will be taken when necessary. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF IGARASHI: MAY DO "SMOOTHING" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO CURB VOLATILITY - BLOOMBERG \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market again to curb volatile yen movements but it won't seek to drive down the yen's value, a senior Finance Ministry official said Thursday, according to Bloomberg News. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: VIETNAM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAY ALLOW COMPANIES TO IMPORT GOLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday that it may allow local companies to import gold in order to stabilize the local gold market, after domestic prices rose to a record high this week. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =INDIA FINANCE SECRETARY SEES HIGHER 'ACCEPTABLE' LEVEL OF INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in India is likely to come down to 6% in the next few months, but the country will have to get used to a higher-than-targeted rate in the medium term, thanks to government initiatives, Finance Secretary Ashok Chawla said Wednesday. (published 0025 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =THAI PM: NO PLAN TO MOVE TO EXCHANGE-RATE TARGETING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand won't target a specific exchange rate for the baht even as the strength of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is trading at a 13-year high, is hurting the country's vital export industry, Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said in an interview Wednesday. (published 2205 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =NZ FINANCE MINISTER: CAN'T TAKE ON MARKET OVER NZ DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's government is largely powerless to prevent the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from appreciating further, adding to pressure on the exports and tourism that its economy depends on, Finance Minister Bill English said Wednesday. (published 2324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA BROAD MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH AT 12-MONTH LOW IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in South Korea's broadest measure of money supply was at its weakest level in a year in August due to a slowdown in foreign fund inflows, data from the Bank of Korea showed Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA MINISTER FERGUSON: MINE TAX COMMITTEE TO REPORT BEFORE CHRISTMAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Resources and Energy Minister Martin Ferguson said Thursday that the Policy Transition Group--the body charged with fine tuning the government's new resources tax--hopes to complete its initial report before the end of December. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA SEPTEMBER PERFORMANCE OF CONSTRUCTION INDEX -2.4 POINTS TO 40.8 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's construction sector contracted in September for the fourth consecutive month, a performance gauge produced by an industry group published Thursday shows. (published 2230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES GROSS INTERNATIONAL RESERVES AT RECORD $53.54 BLN END-SEP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' gross international reserves rose to a record high of $53.54 billion at the end of September, bolstered by the government's bond sales and a foreign loan, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NEW 10-YEAR JGBS MEET FAIR DEMAND ON BACK OF BOJ EASING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New 10-year Japanese government bonds received fair demand at an auction Thursday as the Bank of Japan's monetary easing increased the attractiveness of the long-term bonds, though the lowest coupon in more than seven years limited aggressive bidding. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: ING BANK AUSTRALIA LAUNCHES A$500M RMBS OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ING Bank Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday launched an A$500 million offering of residential mortgage-backed securities. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CANADIAN IMPERIAL BANK OF COMMERCE\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRICES A$750M COVERED BONDS - LEAD MANAGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian Imperial Bank Of Commerce on Thursday priced A$750 million of three-year covered bonds, the first such issue in the domestic market since 2007. (published 0539 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: BOJ FIRES AT YEN, BUT WILL HIT DOLLAR INSTEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan stole a march on the U.S. Federal Reserve this week, in part because of concern over the strong yen -- but, ironically, the move will likely drag the dollar down further against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: MAS SET TO STAND PAT AS SINGAPORE DOLLAR SOARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The sizzling Singapore dollar is a good reason for the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stand pat at its monetary policy meeting next week. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: AUSSIE DOLLAR EVER CLOSER TO ITS DANCE WITH PARITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar against the U.S. greenback, the world's fourth most-traded \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair, is about to dance with parity. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR FALLS VS YEN, NEARS FRESH 15-YEAR LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar edged lower against the yen in nervous trading in Asia Thursday, lurking near 15-year lows against the yen as weak U.S. economic data pointed to further monetary easing by the Fed, pushing Treasury yields lower. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS RISE AS UPSIDE HEDGES SOUGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options rose in Tokyo Thursday as the underlying exchange rate marked a 15-year low of Y82.75 overnight, prompting market participants to hedge against the near term risk of the rate sharply rising. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 07-10-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101007e6a7000cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
