10%/11.80% Wednesday in New York. Spot falls below 82.87 overnight, level hit just before \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sept. 15; may have prompted investors to buy hedges against pair's expected sharp rise on possible additional round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo in near term. Options dealer at major brokerage in Tokyo says multiple players buy 1-week USD-call/JPY-put contracts at strike price of 84.50 with varying volatilities (14.25%, 14.00%, 13.85%, 13.73%). Says those deals amount to $120 million altogether. Says vols may rise to 11.85 if spot extends falls to 82.50.(kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0416 GMT [Dow Jones] Japan MOF sells Y2.0073 trillion of 0.8% 10-year bonds with lowest price of 99.60 yielding 0.843%, in-line with market expectations; bid-to-cover ratio at 2.85 vs 3.16 at previous auction in September, while tail shorter at 0.04 vs 0.10 at last tender. Auction results were fair, supported by dealers' short-covering, but investor demand not too strong due to extremely low yields (new issue carries lowest coupon since June 2003), caution ahead of key U.S. nonfarm payroll data due Friday, says Deutsche Securities strategist Makoto Yamashita. Lead December JGB futures last down 0.19 at 143.96.(megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0414 GMT [Dow Jones] Even if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to conduct another round of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , USD/JPY unlikely to rise as much as it did in September 15, says Minoru Shioiri, chief manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities. Reckons many short-term hedge funds have set up their portfolio to make quick gains on any USD/JPY rises. Expects hedge funds to sell into strength (if MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  again) to cash out; "they have made \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  options portfolio in a way that could help them to make money on the dollar's rise against the yen. So they are actually eagerly waiting for Japan's action." Pair last at 82.91.(takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com) [ 10-07-10 0053ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101007e6a700034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
