\par \par \uc2 0323 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares +0.9% at 465.02, off earlier high at 467.28, with investors buying on hopes banks will cut interest rates from October 15 to boost lending as current high rates discouraging companies from borrowing. "More players are optimistic that inflows will increase from the middle of this month after banks start lowering their rates to attract more borrowers," says brokerage trader. Adds strong foreign buying recently also a positive factor. Volume thin with 27 million shares valued at VND700 billion traded so far. Among advancers, \uc2 Bao Viet Holdings\uc2  (BVH.VH) +5% at VND63,000, \uc2 PetroVietnam\uc2  Fertilizer (DPM.VH) +4.8% at VND32,900, Masan (MSN.VH) +3.9% at VND53,500. Tips immediate resistance at 468. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0321 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 HSBC\uc2  Chief Economist Paul Bloxham tips RBA to hike in November after strong jobs numbers. Bloxham's views being closely followed given he's just left \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 12 years as an analyst, he was also among six economists out of 25 who correctly forecast RBA would pause this week. Says CPI and credit data and will be key, but November looks likely. "We also think that any further appreciation of the exchange rate will increasingly play into the decision process for November." (enda.curran@dowjones.com) [ 10-07-10 0012ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101007e6a70002r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
