\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  reserves hit record high after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 01:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Y2.1 trln \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushes up \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves\par \par \uc2 * Gains in gold prices, euro vs dollar also contribute\par \par \uc2 * Record reserves highlight imbalances from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Kaori Kaneko\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves surged to a record in September after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling the yen for the first time in more than six years, drawing unwanted attention to imbalances created by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Policymakers are at odds over the global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system and tension is mounting ahead of Group of Seven and International Monetary Fund meetings starting on Friday.\par \par \uc2 U.S. officials are pushing for China to allow the yuan to rise faster but China has so far resisted, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation would hurt its economy.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has warned of the risks of competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation, while France has been pushing for a new approach to managing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japan's efforts to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  put it in an akward position because it also supports yuan appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The accumulation of dollar reserves could also contribute to capital flows that push up emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it depresses yields on Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL IMBALANCES\par \par \uc2 "I don't think it's a good idea for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pile up reserves," said Tohru Sasaki, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Sasaki said this was leading to certain imbalances that could be harmful for the global economy.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think Japan will be under strong criticism at the G7 meeting. But at the same time, other countries will argue that if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could be a problem."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves rose to a record $1.1 trillion at the end of September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Japan spent 2.1249 trillion yen ($25.61 billion) on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the month to Sept. 28, the ministry announced previously, as the strong yen against the dollar threatened to derail Japan's slowing economy and worsen deflation.\par \par \uc2 But those actions prompted only temporary gains in the dollar, which fell further against the yen to hit a fresh 15-year low on Wednesday. Market players have grown cautious that Japan may step into the market again.\par \par \uc2 The bulk of Japan's reserves are believed to be held in Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 Japan's foreign reserves also swelled as gains in gold prices inflated the value of the government's holdings, the ministry said. Gold was at $1,307 per ounce at the end of September, up from $1,246 at the end of August, it said.\par \par \uc2 Gains in the euro against the dollar pushed up the value of euro-denominated assets after they were converted into the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.3635 at the end of September versus $1.2679 at the end of August.\par \par \uc2 In the face of growing evidence that the yen's strength was hurting the economy, the Bank of Japan on Tuesday carried out what Governor Masaaki Shirakawa described as "comprehensive monetary easing", pledging to pump more funds into the struggling economy and keep interest rates virtually at zero. ($1=82.93 Yen) (Additional reporting by Stanley White; Editing by Edmund Klamann)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101007e6a600001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
