\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Steps countries are taking to counter hot money\b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2010\par 09:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Oct 6 (Reuters) - More governments around the world are moving to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating as investors, turning their backs on low interest rates in developed economies, pour money into higher-yielding markets.\par \par \uc2 Rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions will be a hot topic for finance ministers from the \uc2 Group\uc2  of Seven industrialised countries who are meeting on Friday and for The International Monetary Fund at its twice-yearly gathering this weekend.\par \par \uc2 The following are recent cases of direct or indirect government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, compiled by Reuters:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  CUTS RATES, \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOR FIRST TIME SINCE 2004\par \par \uc2 * Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly pledges to pump more funds into the economy on Oct 5, launches "comprehensive monetary easing", keeps rates virtually at zero.\par \par \uc2 * Authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Sept. 15, first time since 2004, to drive down yen, selling estimates 2 trillion yen. Figures later show Sept. sales total 2.1249 trillion yen ($25.37 billion)\par \par \uc2 * Prime minister signals Tokyo ready to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Yen fell 3 pct on first day of gov't yen selling\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/fac44p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/fac44p}}}\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL TAKES MORE AGGRESSIVE ACTION\par \par \uc2 * Brazil warns of "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war", doubles tax on foreigners buying local bonds\par \par \uc2 * Brazil sovereign fund yet to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Brazil authorises sovereign wealth fund to buy dollars\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps up daily dollar auctions\par \par \uc2 * Government dismisses chatter of capital controls\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nN05219921] [ID:nN20102448] [ID:nN23213114] [ID:nLDE68R0AT]\par \par \uc2 SWITZERLAND HOLDS OFF ON \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank spent nearly 200 bln Sfr via \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from March 2009\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped in June of this year\par \par \uc2 * Traders speculate \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  move could prompt SNB to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Swiss franc flirting with parity against dollar\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nLDE68D1IK]\par \par \uc2 CHILE WARNS ON PESO, NO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  YET\par \par \uc2 * Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ups rate 50 bps, eyes on peso\par \par \uc2 * Peso trading around same level that triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2008\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues threats but reluctant to act\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nSGO002032]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA SPOTTED BUYING DOLLARS\par \par \uc2 * Authorities repeatedly spotted buying dollars to curb the pace of appreciation in the won. Won currently at highest level since May.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose more than $4 billion in September to a record level of $290 billion.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nTOE66R00T] [ID:nTOE690069]\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINES NOT COUNTERING PESO MOVEMENT AGAINST DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank says taking no action to alter movement of peso, at highest in more than two years\par \par \uc2 * Says liquidity flows are manageable, no imposition of capital controls being considered\par \par \uc2 -- Story link [ID:nMNA002910]\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  WIDENS RANGE OF MATURITIES\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank says unworried about capital inflows, will try to manage rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank introduced a minimum holding period for its bills in June by offering a wider range of maturities\par \par \uc2 * Investors must hold the bills for minimum of one month\par \par \uc2 -- Story links [ID:nJAK536689] [ID:nSGE65F0BV] [ID:nJAK210755]\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  BUYS DOLLARS\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says government to offer incentives for companies to keep dollars abroad\par \par \uc2 * Colombia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps rate stable, eyes peso\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  starts buying at least $20 million daily\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say move insufficient, other measures expected\par \par \uc2 * Accumulation of reserves to last at least four months -- Story links: [ID:N05223485] [ID:nN20274631] [ID:nN15183902] [ID:nN15145483] [ID:nN24212097]\par \par \uc2 PERU EASES GRIP ON FUND OUTFLOWS\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank orders new rise in minimum deposit requirements\par \par \uc2 * Pension funds allowed to hold more assets abroad\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading near two-year high against dollar\par \par \uc2 * Peru's sol to be boosted by 6-7 pct growth in 2011\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:n29245369] [ID:nN14108242]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITED AS LEU FIRMS\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly since late 2008\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nLDE68D0W7]\par \par \uc2 THAILAND TRYING TO SLOW BAHT GAINS\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank worried about baht's 13-year high, studying ways to control inflows\par \par \uc2 * Announces well flagged measures on Sept 23 to encourage outflows\par \par \uc2 * Baht one of Asia's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nSGE694083] [ID:nSGE68K083] [ID:nSGE68M0C9]\par \par \uc2 LINKS\par \par \uc2 - TAKE A LOOK [G7/G8]\par \par \uc2 - Asia's controls [ID:TOE68F05F]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2 /CONTROLS (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|J|NAT|UKI|G|RNP|DNP|PTD|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101006e6a6000ep\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
