\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar May Keep Falling Vs Yen On Fed Easing Views\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2010\par 07:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar was little changed against the yen in Asia on Wednesday but the greenback's gradual fall may continue on views that the Federal Reserve will take additional monetary easing measures in the near term.\par \par \uc2 "After all, the main factor to trade the dollar against the yen now is the U.S. monetary policy outlook," said Sumino Kamei, a senior strategist at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2 The next meeting of the policy-making U.S. Federal Open Market Committee is scheduled for Nov. 2 and Nov. 3, and many investors speculate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will loosen its policy further to help forestall a slowdown in the economy.\par \par \uc2 To gauge how likely a Fed move is, investors will pay close attention to U.S. economic indicators due this week, including \uc2 Automatic Data Processing\uc2 's national employment report for September due at 1215 GMT.\par \par \uc2 A Dow Jones poll of economists forecasts that payrolls will increase by 20,000 after falling by 10,000 in August.\par \par \uc2 If the data miss expectations, investors will start selling the greenback more aggressively, targeting Y82.90, a level close to a point where \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Markets will check if Japanese authorities will step into the market again there, and if not, investors may try to send the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to the psychologically-important level of Y80.00.\par \par \uc2 Although Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda has repeatedly said Japan will act when necessary, a view is intensifying that Tokyo cannot again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- at least this week, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 They note that the current pace of the yen's gains is very moderate, meaning if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this stage, its purpose would clearly be to push down the yen's value, rather than to smooth out excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 This appears especially difficult ahead of a meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from the \uc2 Group\uc2  of Seven leading industrialized nations in Washington on Friday where Noda will be meeting his colleagues and will not want to have to answer difficult questions on Japan's intentions.\par \par \uc2 "Many nations want to have their local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  cheap nowadays to prop up exports and their economies. Japan alone can't make the terms of trade favorable to itself," said Tsutomu Soma, a senior dealer at \uc2 Okasan Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As of 0450 GMT, the dollar stood at Y83.17 from Y83.18 on Tuesday in New York.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the euro was at $1.3840 from $1.3835 and Y115.09 from Y115.11 overnight. Investors said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should strengthen further due to investors' pessimistic views toward the U.S. economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index traded at 77.763 from 77.811 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par  \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              83.13-15   83.19-22   -0.07  83.26   83.08   -10.69 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.3844-49