\par\par \b \uc2 UK MORNING BRIEFING:FTSE Advance To Continue As Mood Improves\b0\par\par\uc2 1,497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2010\par 06:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SNAPSHOT: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Shares seen up; gilts unchanged; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in ranges; gold up, oil lower\f28 \par \par \uc2 -UK Sept Shop Prices Accelerate On Higher Food Costs-Survey\par \par \uc2 -UK Demand For Staff Eases On Public Sector Slowdown - Survey\par \par \uc2 -\uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2 , BHP Continue To Work Through Regulatory Process For JV -Rio\par \par \uc2 -\uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2 , BHP Iron Ore Venture Plan Near Collapse -Report\par \par \uc2 -Rio Denies Making Final Decision To Abandon BHP Joint Venture\par \par \uc2 -Barriers To BHP's Potash Deal Fading But Shareholder Opposition Remains\par \par \uc2 -\uc2 Allied Irish Banks\uc2  To Sell M&T Stake In Public Offering\par \par \uc2 -Rolls-Royce Wins THB6 Bln Engine Deal From \uc2 Thai Airways\uc2  - Report\par \par \uc2 -UK Man Killed By Drone In Pakistan Was Set To Be Terror Chief -Report\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHARES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are likely to bid London shares higher Wednesday, with risk aversion receding slightly. Ahead of the open, IG Markets is calling the FTSE up 25 points at 5660.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "For now, the markets remain in buoyant mood," said Kathleen Brooks, research director at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .com. "The market is currently positioned for a weak [U.S. September] payrolls number. It will be interesting to see if this stance remains as we get closer to Friday. If investors start to get nervous we could see some upward pressure on the greenback."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 David Jones at \f28 \uc2 \f2 IG Index\f28 \uc2 \f2  added, "a degree of caution should probably be attached to these gains. The start of the U.S. earnings season and nonfarm payrolls later this week both have the potential to disappoint."\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  majors were trading in tight ranges in Asia after the dollar's losses Tuesday. Yen traders remained on watch for possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Japanese authorities as dollar/yen edged closer to 82.87, the level at which \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen in September.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell sharply Tuesday against the euro and dropped to its lowest point versus the yen since \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as investors' attention turned to global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actions targeted at propping up slowing economies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sterling, higher against the dollar in Asia, looks to remain firm, underpinned by negative dollar sentiment, higher investor risk appetite, and the surprise rise in the U.K. services PMI. Against the euro, sterling is likely to consolidate around current levels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GILTS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gilts may start little changed Wednesday and seem capped as hopes of additional Bank of England asset purchases this year dimmed somewhat as Tuesday's data showed an improvement in the U.K. services sector. However, lingering expectations of additional Federal Reserve easing keep the downside limited.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices were down Wednesday in Asian trade as forecasts of a massive increase in U.S. crude stockpiles tempered market sentiment following recent rallies, analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York's main contract, light sweet crude for delivery in November fell 15 cents to $82.67 a barrel, while Brent North Sea crude for November delivery shed seven cents to %84.77.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data released by the American Petroleum Institute Tuesday showing a spike in U.S. crude reserves was checking oil prices, said Victor Shum, senior principal of Purvin and Gertz international energy consultants in Singapore.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The API report indicated crude stockpiles climbing by 4.4 million barrels in the last week. That's a huge gain," added Shum.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The crude slump comes on the heels of recent rallies in the oil market, but Shum said prices would continue to be supported by a disruption in oil supply in the U.S. Gulf Coast and a rolling strike in a key French oil terminal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par METALS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Metals were all rallying Wednesday in response to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves to inject ever increasing amounts of liquidity into global markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold hit a record high of $1,344.20 a troy ounce, while copper was at its highest level since July 2008 at $8,250 a metric ton as metals traders reacted to a weak dollar and the likelihood of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action, rather than fundamentals. It was last at $1,343.90 per troy ounce, up $3.30 from its New York close on Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's a money war. Everything is moving up in tandem: gold, copper, equities. It seems every major country wants a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and metals are getting bid higher as a result," said a precious metals trader at a Japanese house in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PRICES: \par  \par DJIA                      10944.72  +193.45   +1.80% \par Nasdaq                     2399.83   +55.31   +2.36% \par S&P 500                    1160.75   +23.72   +2.09% \par FTSE 100                   5635.76   +79.79   +1.44% \par FTSE 250                  10681.96  +118.15   +1.12% \par DJ UK Smaller Companies     904.51    +6.23   +0.69% \par Above are closing prices \par  \par Nikkei 225                 9661.59  +142.83   +1.50% \par S&P/ASX 200                4688.40   +81.51   +1.77% \par Shanghai Comp               Closed \par Dow Future                10877.00   +13.00    +0.1% \par NASDAQ Future              2020.50    +2.00    +0.1% \par S&P Future                 1156.00    +1.30    +0.1% \par Above are as of 0425 GMT \par  \par USD/JPY                   83.13-15            -0.07% \par Range                        83.26   83.08 \par EUR/USD                  1.3844-49            +0.07% \par Range                       1.3858  1.3823 \par GBP/USD                  1.5917-18            +0.22% \par Range                       1.5917  1.5885 \par EUR/GBP                  0.8696-00            -0.13% \par Range                       0.8712  0.8689 \par Above are as of 0350 GMT vs NY close \par  \par Asian Spot Gold           $1343.90    +$3.30   +0.3% \par Comex Gold                $1344.00    +$4.60   +0.4% \par Brent Crude Oil             $84.77    -$0.07   -0.1% \par Above are as of 0400 GMT vs NY close \par  \par CORPORATE CALENDAR: \par  \par Artisan (UK) (ART.LN) : Full year 2010 Preliminary results \par Aurora Investment Trust (ARR.LN) : Interim 2011 Results \par BSS \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BTSM.LN) : Trading statement \par Dunelm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (DNLM.LN) : Interim Management Statement \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 EasyJet\f28 \uc2 \f2  (EZJ.LN) : September Traffic Statistics \par Grainger (GRI.LN) : Full year 2010 Trading statement \par Greggs : Interim Management Statement \par Marston's : Full year 2010 Trading statement \par Redhall \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RH