\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: U.S. Summary\b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2010\par 23:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Energy Service\par \uc2 NRG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 2105 GMT [Dow Jones] U.S. SUMMARY: USD fell sharply against EUR, dropped to lowest point vs JPY since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors' attention turned to global \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions targeted at propping up slowing economies; "Clearly this day has revolved around quantitative easing," said Andrew Busch, global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BMO Capital Markets in Chicago. EUR/USD at 1.3835 late Tuesday from 1.3690 late Monday, USD/JPY at 83.18 vs 83.44, EUR/JPY strengthened to 115.11 vs 114.20, GBP/USD at 1.5896, vs 1.5837, USD/CHF at 0.9671 vs 0.9721. USD Index at 77.811 vs 78.439. Stocks rallied to 5-month high, boosted by encouraging services-sector data, hopes global central banks will follow Japan's lead in stimulating economic growth. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  +3.4%, while \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  +3.1% and DuPont +3%. Dow +1.8%, Nasdaq +2.4%, Philly semicons +2.3%.\par \par \uc2  Treasurys maturing in next three to 10 years rose modestly as signs continued to pop up that global economic recovery is slowing, leaving investors convinced Fed will have to extend more support to economy; 3-year yields down 1.6 bps to 0.592%, 10-year yields down 0.1 bp to 2.476%. December Comex gold rose $23.50 to $1,340.30/oz as investors fled paper \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of metal as a perceived store of value. Crude oil futures climbed, spurred by weakness in dollar, strength in equities. November Nymex crude settled at $82.82/bbl. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjo