\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2010\par 12:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU: DEPRESSED CORPORATE INVESTMENT THREATENS ECONOMIC GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lower levels of business investment and declining wages could weigh on the economic recovery in Europe, the European Commission said Tuesday in its quarterly report on the euro-zone economy. (published 0930 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S PLACES IRELAND ON REVIEW FOR DOWNGRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service Tuesday said it may cut Ireland's debt rating again, citing the increased cost to the government of repairing the stricken banking system, weak economic growth and rising borrowing costs. (published 0922 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE GROWTH SLOWING, RETAIL SALES DROP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone economic growth slowed sharply in September as contractions in peripheral countries such as Spain and Ireland threatened the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area's recovery, a survey by financial information company Markit showed Tuesday. (published 0959 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK SEPT PMI SERVICES EASES DOUBLE DIP FEARS, OUTLOOK MUTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K.'s dominant services sector expanded at a faster pace in September than August, calming fears over a double-dip recession, but the outlook remains muted as uncertainty over public-sector spending cuts continued to weigh on new business, data showed Tuesday. (published 0910 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SURPRISES WITH AMBITIOUS EASING; IMPACT DOUBTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank Of Japan announced an ambitious monetary easing Tuesday that returns to a near zero-rate policy, establishes a Y5 trillion fund to buy private- and public-sector assets, and targets longer-term interest rates in a bid to stimulate the economy. (published 1055 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU REHN:LACK OF YUAN APPRECIATION MAY HURT EU RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro area's economic recovery may suffer if the euro continues to appreciate against the Chinese renminbi and other major world \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , European Economic and Monetary Affairs Commissioner Olli Rehn said Tuesday, urging China to let the value of the renminbi rise significantly. (published 0954 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LOOKS TO EXPLAIN REASONS FOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO G-7 \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister indicated Tuesday that he will try to rally support from other nations at the upcoming Group of Seven meeting in Washington for the government's recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 1001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RUSSIA'S KUDRIN SEES 4% ANNUAL GDP GROWTH THROUGH 2013 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russian Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin said Tuesday the country's gross domestic product will rise "moderately," in the near future, gaining about 4% in 2010 and in each of the next three years. (published 0910 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOF OFFICIAL:GERMANY WILLING TO GIVE UP IMF QUOTA IF OTHERS FOLLOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany wants a packaged solution for the reform of the International Monetary Fund at a meeting this weekend in Washington and it is willing to give up some of its quota if others, such as the U.S., are willing to back down, a German finance ministry official said Tuesday. (published 1030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S LIFTS TURKEY RATINGS OUTLOOK, UPS FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service Inc. on Tuesday lifted Turkey's sovereign outlook and raised its growth expectations for the economy, citing an "unexpectedly robust recovery," but the ratings agency cautioned that an upgrade would depend on the strengthening of fiscal fundamentals in the run-up to national elections due next year. (published 0824 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBA SURPRISES WITH ON HOLD VERDICT BUT KEEPS DOOR OPEN FOR HIKES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised financial markets Tuesday by keeping official interest rates on hold for a fifth straight month, but it left in place a clearly defined tightening bias that could still see the monetary policy brakes tapped again in coming months. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPANESE, CHINESE LEADERS MEET IN SIGN OF DIPLOMATIC THAW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan met with Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao in Brussels Monday, in a crucial sign that recently frosty relations between the two Asian giants are beginning to thaw. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBI GOKARN: CHALLENGE TO KEEP INFLATION UNDER CHECK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  deputy governor, Subir Gokarn, said Tuesday that the main challenge for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains to keep inflation under check. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOLID AUSTRALIA RETAIL SALES LIKELY TO KEEP RBA ON TRACK FOR HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian retail sales grew at a solid pace in August, keeping the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  on track to announce its first hike in interest rates since May later Tuesday. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW CHINA GROWTH PLAN TO MODERATE COMMODITIES DEMAND-ECONOMIST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commodities demand in China will likely moderate somewhat as the country's new growth model moves away from infrastructure and towards high-tech industries, a senior economist said Tuesday. (published 0910 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HK MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY EXPANDS FOR 14TH MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's manufacturing activity expanded for the 14th consecutive month in September due to growth in new orders, indicating a continued strengthening in business conditions in the city, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : SEPTEMBER CPI PROVIDES POLICY 'LEEWAY' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that the deceleration of domestic inflation in September provides authorities flexibility in calibrating monetary policy. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : POLICY STANCE APPROPRIATE GIVEN SEPTEMBER CPI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine inflation rate in September supports the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's benign inflation outlook and reinforces the view the current monetary policy stance is appropriate, Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas Governor Amando Tetangco said Tuesday. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : STUDYING IF NEW MEASURES TO CURB INFLOWS NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  is studying whether additional measures to curb capital inflows are needed, Senior Director Wongwatoo Potirat said Tuesday. (published 0519 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CANADIAN IMPERIAL BANK OF COMMERCE\f28 \uc2 \f2  MANDATES BANKS FOR A$ COVERED BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian Imperial Bank Of Commerce has mandated lead managers for its inaugural issue of Australian dollar-denominated covered bonds, which will be backed by Canada's national housing agency, a lead manager said Tuesday. (published 2323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par FOCUS: EUROPE RAMPS UP CRITICISM OF CHINA'S YUAN POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European policy makers on Tuesday ramped up pressure on China to allow its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen, claiming the yuan's weakness threatens Europe's economic recovery. (published 1033 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ TO STAND PAT IN LATE OCTOBER; FURTHER EASING EYED - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's policy board is expected to keep its super-easy monetary policy steady at its next meeting Oct. 28, though many analysts expect further easing action ahead. (published 0951 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOE WATCH: MPC MAY SPLIT THREE WAYS ON POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England's Monetary Policy Committee is expected to keep policy hold yet again when it meets Wednesday and Thursday, but its members may split into three distinct camps for the first time since August 2008. (published 0847 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: POLICY DIVIDE MAKES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LESS PREDICTABLE \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forecasting just became even more unpredictable. (published 0835 GMT) [ 05-10-10 1058GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101005e6a5000w8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
