\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Looks To Explain Reasons For  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To G-7\b0\par\par\uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2010\par 12:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister on the coming G-7 meeting and the nation's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , plus additional background.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister indicated Tuesday that he will try to rally support from other nations at the upcoming Group of Seven meeting in Washington for the government's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from the G-7 group of leading industrialized nations plan to gather in Washington on Friday in what will be their first face-to-face get-together since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Sept. 15 to help curb the yen's strength. Investors are paying close attention to the meeting, as it could make it easier for Tokyo to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if other major economies show support for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 "I'd like to have a great deal of debate over various challenges regarding the global economic recovery," Yoshihiko Noda said at a regular news conference. "As part of that, there will be such discussions (over \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month) if necessary."\par \par \uc2 Noda also said he wants to "seize the opportunities and hold (such) discussions using various channels." His plan suggests he may also look for individual meetings with other nations' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs, or take advantage of International Monetary Fund meetings to be held in Washington over the weekend, to make a case for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Noda's latest remarks underscore \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hope to tame international criticism against its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan's administration has publicly promised to prevent rapid appreciation in the yen, making it necessary for it to gain an international go-ahead for fighting undue yen rises through--if necessary--\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Should other economies grumble aloud about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action, that could embolden speculators to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher, hurting the nation's export-reliant economy.\par \par \uc2 Noda has insisted over recent weeks that the U.S. dollar's fall was too rapid and that Japan's moves were in line with a G-7 principle against excessive fluctuation in exchange rates. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sept. 15 to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in more than six years, after the dollar continued its months-long downtrend and hit a 15-year low of Y82.87 early that day.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Treasury and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have so far kept silent on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But some key international players have voiced concern.\par \par \uc2 World Bank President Robert Zoellick, though he didn't single out Japan, told the Wall Street Journal in an interview Monday that foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fights are among the issues warranting particular attention. Late last month, IMF Managing Director Dominique Strauss-Kahn noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other countries "have nothing to gain" by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets. Other critics include Eurogroup Chairman Jean-Claude Juncker and U.S. Democratic Representative Sander Levin, who chairs the powerful House Ways and Means Committee that has power over taxes and trade policy.\par \par \uc2 The development made Japan the first G-7 nation of late to act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The U.S. and Europe, seemingly content with their weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have maintained their benign neglect, while developing Asian economies have constantly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend their export-led growth.\par \par \uc2 Speculation is that Noda may emphasize to the G-7 that Japan, unlike China, isn't trying to keep exchange rates at certain levels so its policy shouldn't be a cause of concern. Economy Minister Banri Kaieda, in an recent interview with Dow Jones Newswires, said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "was an emergency escape, a temporary measure." Tokyo doesn't "intend to artificially skew the market through continued (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," Kaieda said.\par \par \uc2 Indeed Japanese officials were quick to welcome additional easing measures taken by the Bank of Japan on Tuesday, as such action helps foster the image that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't relying too much on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the BOJ cut its policy interest rate to virtually zero and announced "comprehensive monetary easing" to spur financial growth, including a Y5 trillion fund to buy private and public sector assets--all of which are strong measures that took financial markets by surprise.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 05-10-10 1001GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101005e6a5000to\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
