\par\par \b \uc2 US To Press  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Issues At IMF - Treasury Official\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael R. Crittenden   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2010\par 17:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--U.S. officials plan to press their foreign counterparts to avoid interfering in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at this weekend's International Monetary Fund meetings, warning of the potential effect on the global rebalancing efforts.\par \par \uc2 A senior Treasury Department official, speaking to reporters at a briefing, said U.S. officials will stress the need for countries to allow for "market-oriented exchange rates" as part of a broader rebalancing of the world economy. Asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the yen, as well as broader volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the official said the U.S. position has not changed.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. has been very consistent that leading economies should be supporting exchange rates based on market fundamentals," the official said.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. believes the IMF should play a more aggressive role in ensuring countries live up to their commitments on exchange-rate policy, the official said, stressing the fund's "very important surveillance mandate."\par \par \uc2 "The IMF has to have an ability to speak forcefully," the official said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues are one of a range of topics finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials are expected to discuss at a series of multi- and bilateral discussions in Washington over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 -By Michael R. Crittenden, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9273; michael.crittenden@dowjones.com [ 10-05-10 1130ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101005e6a5000a3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
