\par\par \b \uc2 Nikkei rises 1.5 pct after surprise BOJ rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2010\par 01:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Nikkei posts biggest percentage gain in almost 3 weeks\par \par \uc2 * BOJ cuts rates, eyes asset buying in surprise move\par \par \uc2 * Market focus moves to U.S. jobs data, Fed's possible easing\par \par \uc2 By Chikafumi Hodo\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 5 (Reuters) - Japan's Nikkei jumped 1.5 percent on Tuesday, its biggest rise in almost three weeks, after the Bank of Japan effectively cut interest rates to zero, weakening the yen and pushing up shares of exporters like \uc2 Sony Corp\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also decided to set up a fund to buy assets ranging from government bonds and short-term government securities to commercial paper and corporate bonds, steps that analysts said would support the market although the long-term impact may be limited.\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ's action was surprising as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered interest rates to zero and expanded the type of assets it will buy, especially assets such as exchange-traded funds (ETFs) and REITs," said Takeshi Osawa, senior fund manager at Norinchukin Zenkyoren Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 "This should prevent share prices from falling sharply from here. The Nikkei should be supported but it is still premature to say that its underlying bearish trend has reversed completely," he said.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Nikkei rose 137.70 points to 9,518.76 and booked its biggest daily percentage gain since Sept. 15 -- when the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in more than six years.\par \par \uc2 The broader Topix rose 9.90 points, or 1.2 percent, to 832.64.\par \par \uc2 But further advances for the Nikkei were blocked by a series of technical resistance levels, including the upper level of the Nikkei's daily Ichimoku cloud around 9,530, as the dollar's recovery against the yen was limited.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was up 0.3 percent at 83.63 yen but off its session high of 83.99 yen reached just after the BOJ's policy announcement. That was still not far from the 15-year low of 82.87 yen set just before \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Sept. 15.\par \par \uc2 The market focus will shift to U.S. payroll data on Friday and the Group of Seven nations meeting later in the week to determine the outlook for the yen.\par \par \uc2 "It's good that the BOJ eased before the Fed took easing steps. It will make it easier for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make a case for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Minori Uchida, senior analyst at the \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2 "But it's probably too much to expect today's steps to fully offset the possible impact of the Fed's eventual quantitative easing. Because Japan's monetary policy has been loose for years, any additional move tends to have a limited impact," Uchida said.\par \par \uc2 KDDI\uc2  JUMPS, MIZUHO REBOUNDS\par \par \uc2 Shares of exporters advanced as the dollar edged up after the BOJ's policy announcement, with \uc2 Sony Corp\uc2  climbing 1.4 percent to 2,600 yen and \uc2 Kyocera Corp\uc2  rising 2.8 percent to 8,340 yen.\par \par \uc2 Konica Minolta\uc2  rose 3.7 percent to 861 yen after CEO \uc2 Masatoshi Matsuzaki\uc2  told Reuters that the company aims to double operating profit from current levels to more than 100 billion yen ($1.2 billion) in the year to March 2014.\par \par \uc2 KDDI Corp\uc2  rose 5.4 percent to 410,000 yen after the nation's No. 2 cellphone operator announced it will launch Japan's first smartphone to feature an electronic money function.\par \par \uc2 The IS 03 phone, to be launched at the end of November, will be manufactured by \uc2 Sharp Corp\uc2 , and use \uc2 Google Inc\uc2 's Android system.\par \par \uc2 Mizuho Financial Group\uc2  rose 3.6 percent to 116 yen, rebounding after revisiting a seven-year low of 110 yen hit on Monday on worries that Japanese banks may be forced to raise fresh capital.\par \par \uc2 Mizuho and other Japanese banks tumbled on Monday after Switzerland tightened the reins on \uc2 UBS\uc2  and \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 , telling them to hold more capital beyond the "Basel III" international standards set three weeks ago. (Additional reporting by Aiko Hayashi; the Tokyo newsroom; Editing by Chris Gallagher)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-JAPAN-STOCKS (UPDATE 6)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101004e6a4001q0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
