\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Quotes on Japan economy by BOJ, govt officials\b0\par\par\uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2010\par 03:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 4 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan is leaning towards easing monetary policy at its two-day meeting ending on Tuesday on growing evidence the stronger yen and slowing overseas growth are undermining a fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2  The BOJ's most likely step will be to further expand a cheap funding tool put in place in December last year that was expanded in March and in August.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to leave its policy rate unchanged at 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2  Following are key quotes by BOJ and government officials on monetary policy and the economy.\par \par \uc2  PRIME MINISTER NAOTO KAN, Oct. 1, policy speech\par \par \uc2  "I hope the BOJ will take further necessary steps aimed at overcoming deflation while working closely with the government."\par \par \uc2  BOJ GOVERNOR MASAAKI SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 27, speech to business leaders in Osaka\par \par \uc2 "Economic trends are not set by \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone but I'm aware that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are one big factor (behind them).\par \par \uc2 "We will hold a policy meeting next week and will guide policy appropriately while watching various points including \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and developments in the U.S. and world economies, and what the reaction is after various stimulus measures expire."\par \par \uc2  SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 26, seminar in Kobe, western Japan\par \par \uc2  "We'll respond (to the need for easing) in a timely and appropriate way."\par \par \uc2  ECONOMICS MINISTER BANRI KAIEDA, Sept. 27, group interview\par \par \uc2  "I don't think it's a good idea to wait to discuss expanding the limits (on the BOJ's JGB holdings) until after they are reached. They should start such discussions now."\par \par \uc2  BOJ BOARD MEMBER RYUZO MIYAO, Sept. 22, news conference\par \par \uc2  (Asked about a possible increase in BOJ purchases of JGBs): "That's one policy option probably under debate at present. But we will not rule out any policy option and won't have preset ideas about our future policy. We will examine the effects and drawbacks of all policy options carefully ...\par \par \uc2  "How we examine effects and drawbacks of policy options changes based on the situations of the economy and prices. How quantitative easing is assessed now may differ from past assessments."\par \par \uc2  SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 16, speech\par \par \uc2  "There is little evidence to support the view that massive expansion in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  balance sheets results in higher inflation in advanced economies."\par \par \uc2  FINANCE MINISTER YOSHIHIKO NODA, Sept. 15, to reporters\par \par \uc2  (On confirming \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted a yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in six years) "We will take decisive steps if necessary, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while continuing to closely watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves from now on."\par \par \uc2  SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 15, in a statement\par \par \uc2  "There has been growing uncertainty about the future, especially for the U.S. economy, and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets have been unstable. In these circumstances, the downside risks to Japan's economy warrant attention.\par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan strongly expects that the action taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will contribute to stable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate formation.\par \par \uc2  "The bank will, while pursuing strong monetary easing, continue to provide ample liquidity to the financial markets."\par \par \uc2  BOJ BOARD MEMBER TADAO NODA, Sept. 15, news conference\par \par \uc2  "We will pursue policy responses depending on moves in the economy and in prices but the BOJ will not consider policy in a manner that links directly to the latest (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) step."\par \par \uc2  SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 7, news conference\par \par \uc2  "We will take the most appropriate action by examining the merits and drawbacks of various steps."  (Reporting by Rie Ishiguro)     \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/BOJ-QUOTES (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101004e6a40001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
